= Picking Up from (28)

When I finished #series-link("20221220-mmo-server-from-scratch(28)-scene-server-update-nif-interfaces", "Starting from Zero: MMORPG Game Server (28)"), the round of physics-engine replacement had wrapped up, and the next step was to rethink how movement sync executes on the client. Crossing terrain with `NavMesh` was already showing problems, and jumping was still waiting to be synced. That was December 20, 2022, and the series went quiet for a long time afterwards.

This post looks back over the whole road. The repository is still `ex_mmo_cluster`, but the mainline running in it is very different from the architecture diagram in #series-link("20220608-mmo-server-from-scratch(0)-introduction", "(0) Introduction"). I want to explain three things: what was built back then, which guesses were later replaced, and why the voxel world is now the single source of truth, why QUIC carries the traffic, and how the cross-Scene handoff that was postponed back then finally got built. The post focuses on server architecture; the client side is discussed only at the concept level.

